alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn main(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "firn, a server of Redis's protocol for the commands apps/firn/README.md lists, over TCP in RESP2 or as inline commands, with pipelining. It serves each accepted client in a context of its own over one keyspace, a shared state every client reaches through atomic statements that hold the entries of the keys a command names, or the keyspace's map whole for DBSIZE. Its invocation, which read_options reads, names up to four arguments by position, the port, how many clients to accept, zero for no limit, the append-only file's name or - for none, and the idle limit, then options by name, --port, --bind, --timeout, --appendonly, --appendfilename, --requirepass and --clients; an invocation that does not read stops firn with status 1. firn listens on the address --bind names, the loopback address by default. An append-only file is replayed before firn listens and every change is appended to it, the file synced once a second. A client silent for the idle limit, when it is not zero, is closed, and while a password is required a client must give it before other commands. Expired keys are removed when a command finds them and by a context that wakes ten times a second.";
